<title>MALAYSIA: Landmarks to take stake in Australian firm.</title>
<headline>Landmarks to take stake in Australian firm.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian hotel company Landmarks Bhd said on Thursday it had proposed to acquire an indirect stake in Australian Hospital Care Ltd (AHC).</p>
<p>In a statement to the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange, Landmarks said it had proposed to acquire a holding company which indirectly owned a 24.6 percent stake in AHC for a cash consideration of 56 million ringgit.</p>
<p>The holding company would be bought from Permodalan Peremba Sdn Bhd, Landmarks said.</p>
<p>AHC is the third largest private hospital operator in Australia, operating 13 hospitals predominantly located in the Melbourne area, said Landmarks.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230 8911)</p>
